{title: O Worship the King}
{artist: Robert Grant / Johann Michael Haydn}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{key_original: G}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]O worship the King, all [G]glorious a[D]bove
O [Bm]gratefully [A]sing His power and His [D]love
Our [D]Shield and De[G]fender, the [D]Ancient of Days
Pa[Bm]vilioned in [A]splendor and girded with [D]praise
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]O tell of His might, O [G]sing of His [D]grace
Whose [Bm]robe is the [A]light, whose canopy [D]space
His [D]chariots of [G]wrath the deep [D]thunderclouds form
And [Bm]dark is His [A]path on the wings of the [D]storm
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The [D]earth with its [G]store of [D]wonders untold
Al[Bm]mighty, Thy [A]power hath founded of [D]old
Hath [D]stablished it [G]fast by a [D]changeless decree
And [Bm]round it hath [A]cast, like a mantle, the [D]sea
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Thy [D]bountiful [G]care, what [D]tongue can recite?
It [Bm]breathes in the [A]air, it shines in the [D]light
It [D]streams from the [G]hills, it de[D]scends to the plain
And [Bm]sweetly dis[A]tills in the dew and the [D]rain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Frail children of [G]dust, and [D]feeble as frail
In [Bm]Thee do we [A]trust, nor find Thee to [D]fail
Thy [D]mercies how [G]tender, how [D]firm to the end
Our [Bm]Maker, De[A]fender, Re[D]deemer, and Friend
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
O [D]measureless [G]Might, inef[D]fable Love
While [Bm]angels de[A]light to worship Thee a[D]bove
The [D]humble cre[G]ation, though [D]feeble their lays
With [Bm]true ado[A]ration shall all sing Thy [D]praise
{end_of_verse}
